\tag{ftip}
\tag{preference}
\tag{provenance}

\card{Remark}{Preference acquisition and judge provenance}{
\p{A preference observation depends on the query presented and the judge who
evaluates it. Concrete elicitation procedures include
\citet{Sections 2.2.2 and 2.2.4}{christiano2017deep} and the language-model
comparison pipeline of \citet{Sections 3.2 and 3.4}{ouyang2022training}.}

\p{The response generator, pair-selection rule, presentation order, judge
population, and aggregation rule can each change the observed law. A later
sample-complexity or population claim must condition on those choices rather
than treating comparison labels as an unqualified source of ground truth.}
}
